      },
      "id": 1,
      "options": {
        "content": "**Tokens and cost count the attempts a provider answered**, with the provider's own token counts and the registry's prices. What a tenant was *charged* (a reservation kept after a failed attempt, for example) is in the gateway's ledger, table `gateway.usage`. The ledger is the record; this dashboard is a view.\n\n**Cost reads 0 on kind.** The simulated `replay` provider is priced at zero in the registry. Cost is above zero only on a route to a priced deployment.\n\n**How a total is computed.** A gateway process exports its counters once a minute, and its first export already carries what it counted, so `increase()` and `rate()` would miss it. Each panel subtracts a series' value at the start of the time range (zero for a process that started inside the range) from its last value. Choose a range of at least two minutes. Prometheus keeps 24 hours on kind, so a longer range shows what it still holds.",
        "mode": "markdown"
      },
      "title": "What these numbers are",
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "description": "Tokens the provider counted for answered attempts, over the selected time range.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "decimals": 0,
          "unit": "locale"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 4,
        "w": 8,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 7
      },
      "id": 2,
      "options": {
        "colorMode": "none",
        "graphMode": "none",
        "reduceOptions": {
